CAT = "ukcarAlert"; SEG = "ALT"
Q = [
("Just before moving off from the side of the road, what final check should you make?",
 "Look round over your shoulder", ["Check your interior mirror again", "Glance at the speedometer", "Check the handbrake warning light"],
 "Mirrors do not cover every area, so the Highway Code says to look round for blind spots and then look round once more just before you move off. Signalling comes before that final check, not after it."),
("What routine should you use before changing speed or direction?",
 "Mirrors, signal, manoeuvre", ["Signal, mirrors, manoeuvre", "Manoeuvre, signal, mirrors", "Signal, brake, manoeuvre"],
 "The Highway Code's reminder is Mirrors, Signal, Manoeuvre. You check what is behind before you signal, so the signal is given only when it is safe and useful."),
("When may you use a hand-held phone while driving?",
 "To call 999 when unsafe to stop", ["While stopped in a traffic queue", "When the road ahead is clear", "For a call lasting under a minute"],
 "You must not use a hand-held phone while driving, including while stationary in traffic. The only exception is calling 999 or 112 in a genuine emergency when it is unsafe or impractical to stop."),
("How long a break does the Highway Code recommend after every two hours of driving?",
 "At least 15 minutes", ["At least 5 minutes", "At least 45 minutes", "At least 1 hour"],
 "Rule 91 recommends a minimum break of at least 15 minutes after every two hours of driving. Plan rest stops into long journeys before tiredness sets in."),
("You feel sleepy on a motorway. Where should you stop to rest?",
 "At the next services", ["On the hard shoulder", "In an emergency area", "On the slip road"],
 "Leave at the next exit or services. The hard shoulder and emergency areas are for emergencies only, and the Highway Code says not to use them to rest."),
("Between which hours are you most likely to feel sleepy on a long drive?",
 "Midnight and 6 am", ["6 am and 10 am", "4 pm and 8 pm", "8 pm and 11 pm"],
 "Rule 91 advises avoiding long journeys between midnight and 6 am, when natural alertness is at its lowest."),
("Another driver flashes their headlights at you. What does the Highway Code say this means?",
 "They are letting you know they are there", ["They are inviting you to pull out now", "They are warning of a police check", "They are giving way to you here"],
 "Rule 110 says headlights should only be flashed to let other road users know you are there. Never assume a flash is an invitation to go; it may be meant for someone else."),
("When must you not use your horn in a built-up area while moving?",
 "From 11.30 pm to 7 am", ["From 10 pm to 6 am", "From midnight to 8 am", "From 9 pm to 7 am"],
 "You must not sound the horn in a built-up area between 11.30 pm and 7 am, unless another road user poses a danger. You must never use it while stationary on the road."),
("A driver behind is following far too closely. What should you do?",
 "Ease off to widen your gap ahead", ["Brake sharply to warn them off", "Speed up to leave them behind", "Wave them past at the next bend"],
 "Dropping back from the vehicle in front gives you more time to brake gently, so the tailgater is less likely to run into you. Braking sharply or speeding up only adds risk."),
("You are driving behind a learner who keeps stalling. What should you do?",
 "Be patient and hold back", ["Sound your horn to hurry them", "Overtake as soon as possible", "Flash your headlights at them"],
 "Rule 217 asks you to be particularly patient with learner and young drivers. Pressure from behind makes mistakes more likely."),
("Your satnav needs reprogramming during a journey. What should you do?",
 "Find a safe place to stop first", ["Do it at the next red light", "Do it while driving slowly", "Do it on a straight road"],
 "Rule 150 says do not be distracted by screen-based navigation and find a safe place to stop before adjusting it. A red light is still driving."),
("Is it safe to use a hands-free phone while driving?",
 "No, it can still distract you", ["Yes, if both hands are on the wheel", "Yes, on roads with low traffic", "Yes, on any motorway"],
 "Hands-free calls are legal but still take your attention off the road. Rule 149 advises against them; let calls go to voicemail and stop safely to return them."),
("You are about to turn right. What should you do just before turning?",
 "Check right mirror and blind spot", ["Check your left mirror only", "Sound your horn as you turn", "Switch on your hazard lights"],
 "Rule 180 says check your mirrors and blind spot before turning right, in case a motorcyclist or cyclist is overtaking you."),
("Why should you take extra care when you see a bus at a stop ahead?",
 "People may step out in front", ["It is likely to reverse", "It may sound its horn at you", "It always pulls out at once"],
 "People getting off a bus may cross in front of it where you cannot see them. Slow down and be ready to stop."),
("When should you give way to a bus signalling to pull out from a stop?",
 "When it is safe to do so", ["Never, you have priority", "Only on bus routes", "Only in the daytime"],
 "Rule 223 asks you to give priority to buses when you can do so safely, especially when they signal to pull away from stops."),
("A driver cuts in sharply in front of you. What should you do?",
 "Ease off and stay calm", ["Flash your headlights", "Drive close behind them", "Sound your horn for long"],
 "Drop back to restore a safe gap and do not retaliate. Rule 147 asks you to be considerate and not to over-react to other road users' mistakes."),
("What is the safest way to pass parked cars on your side of the road?",
 "Give way to oncoming traffic", ["Speed up to pass before them", "Flash at oncoming drivers", "Sound your horn as you pass"],
 "The obstruction is on your side, so oncoming traffic normally has priority. Hold back and leave room for a car door opening or a child stepping out."),
("How should you deal with a long queue merging into one lane at road works?",
 "Merge in turn at low speed", ["Close the gap so no one cuts in", "Use the hard shoulder", "Stop and wave everyone in"],
 "Rule 134 recommends merging in turn when traffic is moving at very low speed, such as approaching road works. Leaving gaps lets the queue flow."),
("What should you do if you are dazzled by the headlights of oncoming traffic at night?",
 "Slow down or stop", ["Flash your main beam back", "Look straight into them", "Speed up to pass quickly"],
 "Rule 115 says that if you are dazzled you should slow down and, if necessary, stop. Flashing back dazzles the other driver too."),
("Why should you check your mirrors before opening your door to get out?",
 "A cyclist may be passing close by", ["To check your parking is straight", "To see if you left lights on", "To check the kerb height"],
 "Rule 239 says check for cyclists and other traffic before opening your door. Using the hand on the opposite side to the door turns your body so you look over your shoulder."),
]
